![EX_11](free_regression/imagens_testes/reg_11.png)


### Observando a loss do modelo no tempo

```python
data = [0, 1]
for _ in range(8):
  data.append(-0.8*data[-1] + 1.2*data[-2])

data = [[i, x] for i, x in enumerate(data)]

def f(x:float, a:float, b:float, c:float, d:float) -> float:
  return a*b**x + c*d**x

modelo = Regression(f, print = True)
modelo.set_seed(1)
modelo.lock(d = data[-1][1]/data[-2][1])

modelo.run(data, save_infos = True)
print(modelo)

import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
loss = modelo.return_loss()

plt.figure(figsize = (10, 4))
plt.plot(loss["iteration"], loss["loss"], alpha = 0.4, zorder = 0, label = "Loss")
plt.plot(loss["iteration"], loss["loss"].rolling(window = 300).quantile(0.2), alpha = .7, zorder = 1, label = "Loss Smoothed")
plt.plot(loss["iteration"], loss["best_loss"], color = "red", linestyle = "--", zorder = 1, label = "Min Loss")
plt.yscale("log")
plt.xlabel("Iteration")
plt.ylabel(r"Loss ($log_{10}$)")
plt.title("Loss")
plt.legend()
plt.show()
```

![EX_loss](free_regression/imagens_testes/image_loss.png)
